Without arguments, print the version of nexoctl. The subcommands manage the
versioning of buckets: enable, suspend, info.

Usage:
  nexoctl version [flags]
  nexoctl version [command]

Available Commands:
  enable      Enable the versioning of a bucket
  info        Show the versioning state of a bucket
  suspend     Suspend the versioning of a bucket

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for version

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl version [command] --help" for more information about a command.
